# Variable names only. Every line is commented out on purpose: Foundry auto-loads a .env file, and an
# empty value for a numeric variable would be a parse error. Uncomment what you need in your own .env
# (git-ignored) or simply export the variable in your shell.
#
# NEVER put a private key, a mnemonic or an RPC URL that contains an API key into a committed file.
# Nothing in this repository reads a private key from the environment.
# Note that forge itself takes the keystore selection from ETH_KEYSTORE, ETH_KEYSTORE_ACCOUNT and
# ETH_PASSWORD when they are set (also from a .env file): leave them unset unless you mean it.

# Fork tests (test/fork/*, checker/test/fork/*), script/probe-priority-fee.sh, script/verify-deploy-local.sh.
# Read-only. A keyless public endpoint is enough (the README names one).
# BASE_RPC_URL=

# Tool locations, only if forge / cast are not on PATH (used by the shell scripts)
# FORGE=
# CAST=

# checker/script/check-hook.sh and checker/test/CheckHook.t.sol (full list: checker/README.md)
# HOOK=
# CHECK_RPC_URL=
# CHECK_FORK_BLOCK=
# CHECK_NATIVE=
# CHECK_REPORT=
# CHECK_STRICT=
# POOL_MANAGER=
# POOL_CURRENCY0=
# POOL_CURRENCY1=
# POOL_FEE=
# POOL_TICK_SPACING=

# script/Mine*HookAddress.s.sol (read-only address mining): POOL_MANAGER above, and optionally
# DEPLOYER=

# script/probe-priority-fee.sh (read-only eth_call probe)
# PROBE_FROM=

# script/verify-deploy-local.sh (local anvil fork only)
# FORK_BLOCK=
# ANVIL_PORT=
